ior margin  0 8cm from the anterior margin  and medial to the stitch with surgical staples  with two adjacent rubbery ill defined nodules measuring 0 5cm in diameter  A second metal clip is identified in the central portion of the specimen  in the 5 o clock position  located 1 3cm from the anterior margin  with no discernible associated lesion  The remainder of the specimen consists predominantly of tan white fibrous breast parenchyma  with multiple blue domed cysts up to 0 3cm in diameter  as well as several areas of parenchymal irregularity and vague rubbery nodularity  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion  1  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion  2  entirely submitted  including area with metal clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening uninvolved parenchyma between Lesion  1 and Lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of parenchyma immediately medial to lesion  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of parenchyma immediately medial to lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion  3  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion  4  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion  5  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of irregular parenchyma from the central portion of the specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined rubbery nodules in the axillary region  near lesion  5   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Region containing second metal clip  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast skin   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm ellipse of unremarkable tan white skin  excised to a maximum depth of 1 2cm  with a central REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm defect  The soft tissue margin of resection is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGN