Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 35 CLINICAL DATA  Mammographic abnormalities                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   1  OUTER MEDIAL   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SOLID  CRIBRIFORM  AND PAPILLARY TYPES  D E I   HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  FOCALLY AT A MARGIN  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  E F   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  WITH MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND A SMALL RADIAL SCAR  BREAST  LEFT   2  OUTER UPPER   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 1 OF 3  CIRCUMSCRIBED NODULE ABUTTING AN INKED MARGIN  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHATIC AND BLOOD VASCULAR INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    LOW GRADE  CRIBRIFORM AND PAPILLARY TYPE  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT TO THE MARGINS OF EXCISION  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 22 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  Specimen  2   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm piece of breast tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette D through M  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm firm  white  ill defined nodule  Representative sections of the nodule are submitted in cassettes A through C  Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST TISSUE  1   NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2   LEFT BREAST TISSUE  2   SMALL LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   1   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  2   EXCISION , Positive.
