 of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision of right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with two surgical sutures the short stitch indicating the superior margin and the long stitch indicating the lateral margin with an attached ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Serial sections of the specimen reveal 1 5cm hemorrhagic previous biopsy cavity surrounded by fibrotic tissue  Grossly no evidence of carcinoma is identified  The previous biopsy cavity is located 1 0cm from the superior margin and 0 6cm from the superficial margin  Section code  A  Previous biopsy to superior  B  Previous biopsy to anterior  C D  Previous biopsy to posterior  E  Fibrotic area posterior to lateral  F  Biopsy to skin  G  Biopsy to medial  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel lymph node level one  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fatty lymph node  bisected and entirely submitted in cassettes H and I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel lymph node level two  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of adipose fatty lymph node bisected and entirely submitted in cassette J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tiss